        <p>question of conversion. This resolution arose upon a query by the Local Government Board, who had been attracted by 'a refereuos in the Medical Officer of Health's annual report, sug- gesting the advisability of tbolishing the pail system in favour of the water r•lnset system. It seems a far cry from sewage to ;:;rks, but our point is that if the Merp-ty (euld he cleared of its pollution, Victoria Park would be bounded on two sides !iy a river giving stretches as attractive to the pedestrian or the rowel' as those possessed by sny river in Eng- land.</p>
