      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-07-11_WidnesExaminer_art0219" n="art0219">
        <head>WATER POLO.</head>
        <p>WATER POLO.</p>
        <p>In the second round for the Lancashire Junior Cup, Warrington meet Accrington away on Monday, and the team will be: Goal, C. Woods; backs, S. Ince and L. Graham; half- back, C. Turner; forwards, H. Sisson, R. Pepper and J. Graham. . .</p>
        <p>_ Next Thursday Warrington entertain Leigh at home, and on the same evening Miss F. Warrington, of Manchester, will give an exhi- bition of trick and fancy swimming. The only match in the second round Of the Works' Competition will take place ,between Whitecross and Crosfield's Juniors, and as Whitecross are the favourites a keen race should be the result.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-07-11_WidnesExaminer_art0220" n="art0220">
        <head>WIDNES DEFEAT RUNCORN.</head>
        <p>WIDNES DEFEAT RUNCORN.</p>
        <p>Widnes and Runcorn met at Widnes Baths on Tuesday evening. Widnes lost the toss and were set to defend the deep end in the first half. At half-time the 'scores were Widnes 4 goals, Runcorn 2. In the second half Widnes had easily the major portion of the game and scored four more goals. Result: Widnes 8 goals, Runcorn 2. Runcorn won the squadron race by half a length. A two lengths club handicap resulted as follows: Wheat 1, Pitt 2, Burgess 3.</p>
      </div>
