      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-07-11_WidnesExaminer_art0223" n="art0223">
        <head>TROPHY FOR THE MUNICIPAL</head>
        <p>TROPHY FOR THE MUNICIPAL</p>
        <p>LEAGUE.</p>
        <p>'Councillor Henry Roberts, having been ap- proached by the officials of the Municipal Bowling Greens' League, who were in quest of a trophy, he very kindly consented to provide a challenge shield. Subscriptions to a fund for the purpose of supplying medals to the winners and runners-up are being asked for, and up to date the Mayor and Sir Gilbert Greenall have responded. The League competitions are creating great enthusiasm, there being an average of eighty players per green striving to gain positions in their. respective teams.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON LIBERAL ' ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>Annual Main.</p>
        <p>The draw for the third section of main for next Saturday is as follows</p>
        <p>Abbreviations.-T.H., Town Hall; 8., Bewsey; W., Whiteeross; 0., Orford; F., Fairfield; L., Latchford; H., Howley; St. A., St. Austin's; St. J., St. John's. PRELIMINARY ROUND. 2.15 to 3 o'clock. 1 W. Rooke, St. A. (3) v. J. Feeney, B. (3). 2. N. Cook, L. (3) v. J. Henegan, W. (3). 3. T. Helsby, St. A. (3) v. G. Monks, F. (1). 4.J. Holcroft, St. J. (4) v. W. Stokes, T.H. (3). 5. A. Weston, St. A. (3) V. J. Cliffe, F. (6). 6. A. Gleave, St. A. (0 1) v J. Baguley, B. (6). 7. J. Oakley, St. A. (5) v. F. Rigby, St. A. (scr.). 8. H..Bennion, St.A. (2) v. J. H. Pepper, St.A.(5) 9.'J. Howard, W. (6) v. H. Parry, W. (1). 10. J. Waring, B. (5) v. T. Jackson, Vere-st. (2). 11. T. Timmins, W. (2) v. B. Lloyd, H. (6). 12. J. Rigby, jun., H. (3) v. G. Clifie, L. (5)• 13. W. Broadhurst, F. (I) v. J. Wood, T.H. (1). 14. J. Griffiths, St. A. (3) v. S. Heekle, F. (6). 15. W. Chilton, T.H. (4) v. A. P. Davies, St.J. (3) 16. J. Holt, St. J. (5) v. J. Hatton, H. (6). 17. W. Lawton, W. (2) v. B. Hall, F. (3). 18. R. Barnett, 0. (6) V. W. Bibby, W. (2). 19. J. Broadhurst, jun. (3) v. F. Davenport, W. (4) 20. M. Flynn, B. (3) v. J. Narraway, W. (6). 21. T. Welsby, W. (2) v. A. Wood, 0., (3).</p>
