      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-07-11_WidnesExaminer_art0234" n="art0234">
        <head>SALES BY AUCTION</head>
        <p>SALES BY AUCTION</p>
        <p>HERBERT JOHNSON, AUCTIONEER AND VALUER,</p>
        <p>BEWS-Ef --CiaIIITERS, WARRINGTON. Sales by Auction of -Freehold and Leasehold Properties, Building Land, Ground Rents. Farming and Trade Stocks, Household Furni- ture, Stocks, Shares, and Debentures. Valuations for Sale, Probate and Mortgage, on reasonable terms. Sale room, Queen-street. invited.</p>
        <p>Consignments</p>
        <p>H. B. HOUGHTON. AUCTIONEER, VALUER, ESTATE AND INSURANCE AGENT, 1, SUEZ-STREET, WARRINGTON. SALES BY AUCTION, VALUATIONS FOR SALE, MORTGAGE OR PROBATE, ESTATES MANAGED. Insurances of every description immediately arranged. Telephone 908.</p>
        <p>HENRY TAYLOR, AUCTIONEER AND VALUER. ESTATE &amp; INSURANCE AGENT. "</p>
        <p>15. BOLD-STREET. WARRINGTON. Tel. 228.</p>
        <p>BY Messrs. A. 11. CLIVE and Co.</p>
        <p>_ PRELIMINARY NOTICE. TO BE SOLD BY AUCTION By /Ur ESSRS A. H. CLIVE &amp; CO., in conjunction JUL with Mr. ROBERT LOWE, at the BLUE BELL INN, Horsemarket-street, Warrington, on WEDNESDAY, the 29th day of JULY, 1914, at 4 p.m., subject to Conditions of Sale to be then produced.</p>
        <p>Lot 1. A pair of well-built Semi-detached Villas, be- ing " Gwenlynn " and " Ethelstone," fronting Warrington-road, Penketh, Warrington, and the land occupied there With. Gross annual rental, £4l.</p>
        <p>Lot 2. All that well-built Detached Dwelling-house known as "Brierfield," fronting to Station-road, Penketh, Warrington, and the land belonging thereto. For further particulars apply to the Auction- eers, and to Messrs. Batty, Ford, and Buckley, Solicitors, 2, Booth-street, Manchester.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-07-11_WidnesExaminer_art0235" n="art0235">
        <head>By Mr. FRANK H. FriLOWS.</head>
        <p>By Mr. FRANK H. FriLOWS.</p>
        <p>"GOLDEN RULE," 87, BUTTERMARKET- STREET, and 24, MERSEY-STREET, WARRINGTON. TO BE SOLD BY AUCTION, entirely without reserve, on the premises, as above on TUESDAY, JULY 14th, 1914, commencing at 10.30, at 24, Mersey-street FRANK H. FELLOWS is instructed to SELL the whole of the Very Useful HOUSE- HOLD FURNITURE and Effects, and the FIXTURES and FITTINGS of the two estab- lishments, comprising Dressing Chests, Brass and Iron Bedsteads, Spring Mattresses, Toilet and Trinket Ware, Wool Beds, Linolawns, Rugs, Carpets, Pictures, Box Ottoman, Orna- ments, Occasional Tables, Chests of Drawers, Overmantels, Kitchen and other Tables, Grand- father Clock, Singer Treadle and Hand Machines, American Organ (11 stops), Piano- forte, Music Stool, Iron Safe, Bronzes, Dresser, Brass Hearth Suites, Fire Brasses, Books,. 2 Cash Tills, large framed Mirrors, expensive Basket Carriage, Outside Blinds and Signs, Gas Fittings, nearly new Outside Lamps, Air-tight Show Cases, well-made Wall Fixtures and Counters, Glass Shelves, and other Items too numerous to mention. Catalogues may be had on the premises, or from the Auctioneer's Offices, 248 and 250, Cor- poration-street, Birmingham. All laid-by goods must be fetched away during the month of July.</p>
      </div>
