        <p>Fat Men's Grievance. Paris boasts of a Sdciety of Fat Persons, and its adipose members have a grievance which has prompted them to petition the Prefect of Police. M. Hennion is reminded in this docu- ment (says the " Globe") that the doors of the motor omnibuses, tramcars, and under- ground trains are only constructed with a view to the passage of travellers of normal girth, and the French Falstaffs therefore demand their en- largement, adding, with a veiled threat, that the fat man is quite as good an elector as his lean fellow-citizen. But if they .have their doors enlarged, it would only be fair and logical to ask them to pay extra for transportation.</p>
